"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph/cliqueExpansion()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/cliqueExpansion()","type":"topic","title":"cliqueExpansion()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cliqueExpansion","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19AdjacencyListModule010UndirectedaB0V","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The clique expansion (XGI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to_graph"},{"type":"text","text":", Berge’s 2-section): every vertex, isolated ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, in vertex-index order, and an edge between every two vertices that share a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge, once, with no self-loops. Edges ascend by (index of u, index of v), u the lower."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Singletons and empty hyperedges add no edge. Lossy and quadratic: one hyperedge of k members"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is k(k − 1)\/2 edges."}],"url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph\/cliqueexpansion()"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph/lineGraph(s:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph\/linegraph(s:)","role":"symbol","title":"lineGraph(s:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/lineGraph(s:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lineGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(